url": "https://en.wikipedia.org/?curid=290527", "text": "is headquartered in Dhahran. Saudi Aramco has both the world's largest proven crude oil reserves, at more than 270 billion barrels (43\nOn 31 January 1944, the company name was changed from California-Arabian Standard Oil Co. to Arabian American Oil Co. (or Aramco). On\n1988. In November 1988, a royal decree created a new Saudi Arab company, the Saudi Arabian Oil Company, to take control of\naviation and diesel needs. Aramco recommissioned 146 Harmaliyah, Khurais, and Ghawar oil wells with associated gas oil separation plants, and saltwater treatment\nMaster Gas System. In 2024, its oil production total was 12.7 million barrels of oil equivalent per day, and it manages over", "retrieved_text_sha256": "50ede48cb2bf39b8768c4f5f173f5d45278078781a3b3eef28e8921cb7e961d1"}], "research": {"event_date": "2026-09-24", "sensitive": false, "claims": [{"id": "c1", "fact": "\u0623\u0631\u0627\u0645\u0643\u0648 \u0627\u0644\u0633\u0639\u0648\u062f\u064a\u0629 \u062a\u0645\u0644\u0643 \u0623\u0643\u0628\u0631 \u0627\u062d\u062a\u064a\u0627\u0637\u064a \u0646\u0641\u0637 \u062e\u0627\u0645 \u0645\u0624\u0643\u062f \u0641\u064a \u0627\u0644\u0639\u0627\u0644\u0645\u060c \u0628\u0623\u0643\u062b\u0631 \u0645\u0646 270 \u0645\u0644\u064a\u0627\u0631 \u0628\u0631\u0645\u064a\u0644\u060c \u0648\u0623\u0643\u0628\u0631 \u0625\u0646\u062a\u0627\u062c \u064a\u0648\u0645\u064a \u0628\u064a\u0646 \u0634\u0631\u0643\u0627\u062a \u0627\u0644\u0646\u0641\u0637 \u0643\u0644\u0647\u0627.", "source_id": "wiki-290527", "quote": "is headquartered in Dhahran. Saudi Aramco has both the world's largest proven crude oil reserves, at more than 270 billion barrels (43", "passage_id": "wiki-290527:p2"}, {"id": "c3", "fact": "\u0641\u064a 31 \u064a\u0646\u0627\u064a\u0631 1944 \u062a\u063a\u064a\u0651\u0631 \u0627\u0633\u0645 \u0627\u0644\u0634\u0631\u0643\u0629 \u0645\u0646 \u00ab\u0643\u0627\u0644\u064a\u0641\u0648\u0631\u0646\u064a\u0627-\u0623\u06